<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end well ahead but lag Bunds.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end well ahead but lag Bunds.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1534 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	106.80/90 (+0.07)	   3.72 (-0.04)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   115.02/12 (+0.21)	   4.52 (-0.05)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.78/88 (+0.33)	   5.50 (-0.05)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   115.18/38 (+0.50)	   6.28 (-0.07)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	102.90 (+0.47)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (Sept)	114.75 (+0.06 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.1260 (prev 1.1259)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.02	+0.03	  10-2 yr  181     (179)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.04	-0.06	  10-5 yr   99	(98)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.05	-0.06</p>
<p>-------------------------(July 17)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds take cue from buoyant Bund futures to push ahead and book solid gains. But Guilders again underperform, with spreads to Germany under pressure. Dollar dip helps market, dealers say next move still uncertain.</p>
